            <div xml:id="d733">

                <pb facs="0686" n="674" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg674"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.24/1512: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-07T16:15:00+01:00">February 7,
                            1944—4:15 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 15—1 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–153. In reply to statements on military supplies for Saudi Arabia, quoted in
                    Department’s A–5 of January 1, Foreign Office has now answered as follows:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Thank you for your letter of the 13th January about military supplies
                            for Saudi Arabia.</p>
                        <p>“We are glad to note that agreement has been reached that such supplies
                            are to be provided in substantially equal measure by the Government of
                            the United States and by His Majesty’s Government.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
